 Every Pashmore piece is hand-spun, handwoven and hand-finished by artisan families in Kashmir. Small irregularities in the weave are the signature of handwork, not a defect."},{"question":"How do I know the Pashmina is genuine?","answer":"Each order ships with a craft certificate recording the fibre grade, the loom it was woven on and the name of the weaver who finished it."},{"question":"Can I return it if the colour is not what I expected?","answer":"Yes. Unused pieces in their original packaging can be returned within 14 days of delivery. Handwoven textiles photograph slightly differently under different light, so we make returns straightforward."}],"rating":{"average":4.8,"count":87},"relatedSlugs":["walnut-brown-mens-wool-shawl","slate-grey-mens-cashmere-stole","heritage-nehru-jacket-charcoal"]}]}],"$L32","$L33"]
